From 21be430b2032b6d6e1535231aeb9381b9d282b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Matched-null band is now a FILTER, not a preference.
 draw_matched_null_masks previously searched within +/-35% and appended the
 closest miss when every try failed, so n_null counted masks rather than
 matched masks and null_quality's K-floor tested the wrong quantity: on the
 real pool a target of 5 fires returned 200 masks of which 141 were out of
 band, fire counts spanning 1 to 424, and the run priced and published them.
 Out-of-band draws are now DISCARDED, chosen over a separate matched-fraction
 gate because it makes the existing K-floor do double duty - n_null IS the
 matched count, one threshold guards both, no second number to keep in step.
 The function returns draw statistics and the matched fraction, rejected
 count, band tolerance and target range now appear on the console line and in
 every catalogue row beside n_null_family. Null direction is drawn from the
 family's own LONG share rather than j%2. clusters_from_entries takes
 signal_ids as a required parameter. The module docstring records that the
 null matches RARITY but not TEMPORAL STRUCTURE, which bears on F1, F2 and F6.

---
 dot_master_discovery/engine/catalogue.py | 90 ++++++++++++++++++------
 dot_master_discovery/engine/selection.py |  2 +-
 dot_master_discovery/master.py           | 22 ++++--
 3 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dot_master_discovery/engine/catalogue.py b/dot_master_discovery/engine/catalogue.py
